  "description": "EEG recordings from 10 healthy participants performing kinesthetic motor imagery of gait while walking with a fully assisted lower-limb exoskeleton on flat ground. Trials alternate between relaxation, motor imagery, and a regressive-count distractor task, with auditory cues. The dataset is part of the DECODED sub-project of EUROBENCH and supports the cognitive assessment of motor imagery in brain-computer interface research.",
  "methods_description": "EEG was recorded with a Brain Products actiCHamp system using 27 EEG channels and 4 EOG channels at 200 Hz. The reference was the left earlobe (A1) and the ground the right earlobe (A2). Online filters were a 0.1 Hz high-pass and a 50 Hz notch. Each session had 16 runs of 9 s cue-based trials with auditory cues.",
